 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 676806,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Why is it important to track customer satisfaction?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1344475,
     "content_html": "We don’t need to; we already have their money.",
     "correctness": "0.0",
     "feedback_html": "That&#8217;s not correct. If you want a customer to do business with you again, it&#8217;s important to track their satisfaction."
    },
    {
     "id": 1344474,
     "content_html": "Customer referrals can be a powerful promotional tool.",
     "correctness": "0.0",
     "feedback_html": "That&#8217;s not correct. Gaining referrals from satisfied customers is just one reason why it&#8217;s important to try customer satisfaction."
    },
    {
     "id": 1344473,
     "content_html": "Customer acquisition can be expensive; repeat purchases can be much more profitable.",
     "correctness": "0.0",
     "feedback_html": "That&#8217;s not correct. Lowering the cost of customer acquisition and retention is just one reason why it&#8217;s important to track customer satisfaction."
    },
    {
     "id": 1344476,
     "content_html": "Statements b and c are both correct.",
     "correctness": "1.0",
     "feedback_html": "We discussed the concept of lifetime customer value (LCV) in the text. Customer acquisition can be very expensive, especially with a missionary sell (e.g., convincing a customer that they have a need for an unknown product or service). Repeat purchases may not require any additional promotional expense. Happy customers also serve as brand ambassadors that spread the word about a company&#8217;s products/services. Negative reviews from brand ambassadors can be extremely damaging&#8212;we want to uncover any problems right away."
    }
   ],
